d 20: In BB with Ad 4s (A4o — weak ace). Hero (SB) folded preflop with K7o. No postflop data.\n\nHand 21: In SB with 7s 6h (suited connector — weak). CALLED preflop. BET flop 3 with middle pair (pair of 7s) on 4s 7c Jd. Hero folded.\n\nHand 22: In BB with Td Th (pocket tens — premium). Hero (SB) folded preflop with 55. No postflop data. BB range confirmed to include strong pocket pairs.\n\nHand 23: In SB with Ad 5s (A5o). CALLED preflop. BET flop 3 on 6c 3c Qs with complete air (A-high, no pair). FIRST OBSERVED BLUFF/AIR C-BET.\n\nHand 24: In BB with 5h 4c (54o — weak offsuit connector). Hero (SB) folded preflop. No postflop data.\n\nHand 25: In SB with Ks 7d (K7o). CALLED preflop. BET flop 3 on 2d Ad Ts with K-high only (no pair). SECOND OBSERVED AIR C-BET.\n\nHand 26: In BB with Kd 5h (K5o — weak king offsuit). Hero (SB) folded J3o preflop. No postflop data.\n\nHand 27: In SB with 8d 2d (82s — EXTREMELY weak). CALLED preflop. BET flop 3 with bottom pair (pair of 8s) on 9c 8s 5s. Hero folded Td 8h.\n\nHand 28: In BB with 8s 9c (89o — weak offsuit connector). Hero folded AA preflop (hero error). No postflop data. Confirms BB range includes weak offsuit connectors.\n\nHand 29: In SB with 9c Jh (J9o — weak offsuit connector). CALLED preflop. BET flop 3 on Ts 4c 7d with gutshot draw (needs 8 for 7-8-9-T), no pair. SEMI-BLUFF / DRAW C-BET confirmed.\n\nHand 30: In BB with 3h 5c (35o — extremely weak offsuit connector). Hero (SB) folded preflop with 2d 6h. No postflop data. Further confirms near-any-two-cards BB range.\n\n===TENDENCIES (30 hands)===\nPREFLOP: Wide/loose range from both blinds. SB raises Ax (ATo x2, A8o, ATs) — raise range ~A8+. SB calls ANY two suited cards down to 82s and offsuit hands like J9o, K3o, K7o — near-unlimited call range. SB folds occasionally (hands 15, 17, 19). BB range spans 35o, 54o/s, 95o, 97o, 89o, K5o, weak aces, premiums — extremely wide, virtually any two cards.\n\nPOSTFLOP (8 hands IP): Bets ANY pair at 100% (3/3). Bets draws/semi-b